    "findings": [
      {
        "title": "Noisy risk numbers",
        "body": "One simulation run is one draw: the structured note's sensitivities swung from run to run. Every gap now comes with an error band, and alerts fire only beyond it."
      },
      {
        "title": "Unstable long-dated market data",
        "body": "Long-dated NVIDIA prices dropped in and out of the data day to day, so the two-year note was often valued on data that stopped short of a year. The engine now keeps a stable curve past two years every day."
      },
      {
        "title": "A model setting that drifted daily",
        "body": "An automatic smoothing choice inside the pricing model changed every day and moved the note's value with it. It is now fixed, measured on every stored day."
      },
      {
        "title": "Observation dates simulated days off",
        "body": "The note's quarterly test dates were simulated up to 5.5 days from the real dates. The simulation now hits every date exactly."
      }
    ]
